#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:91
msgid "Any information you provide will not be shared with service providers without your authorization."
msgstr "Any information you provide will not be shared with service providers without your authorisation."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:90
msgid "You may need to first sign up for an account with the service that you plan to use. When you do so, you would need to authorize Contact Form 7 to access the service with your account."
msgstr "You may need to first sign up for an account with the service that you plan to use. When you do so, you would need to authorise Contact Form 7 to access the service with your account."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:89
msgid "On this screen, you can manage services that are available through Contact Form 7. Using API will allow you to collaborate with any services that are available."
msgstr "On this screen, you can manage services that are available through Contact Form 7. Using the API will allow you to collaborate with any services that are available."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:87
msgid "There are also special mail-tags that have specific names, but do not have corresponding form-tags. They are used to represent meta information of form submissions like the submitter&#8217;s IP address or the URL of the page."
msgstr "There are also special mail-tags that have specific names, but do not have corresponding form-tags. They are used to represent meta information of form submissions like the submitter&#8217;s IP address or the URL of the page."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:86
msgid "A mail-tag is also a short code enclosed in square brackets that you can use in every Mail and Mail (2) field. A mail-tag represents a user input value through an input field of a corresponding form-tag."
msgstr "A mail-tag is also a short code enclosed in square brackets that you can use in every Mail and Mail (2) field. A mail-tag represents a user input value through an input field of a corresponding form-tag."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:84
msgid "While form-tags have a comparatively complex syntax, you do not need to know the syntax to add form-tags because you can use the straightforward tag generator (<strong>Generate Tag</strong> button on this screen)."
msgstr "While form-tags have a comparatively complex syntax, you do not need to know the syntax to add form-tags because you can use the straightforward tag generator (<strong>Generate Tag</strong> button on this screen)."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:83
msgid "A form-tag is a short code enclosed in square brackets used in a form content. A form-tag generally represents an input field, and its components can be separated into four parts: type, name, options, and values. Contact Form 7 supports several types of form-tags including text fields, number fields, date fields, checkboxes, radio buttons, menus, file-uploading fields, CAPTCHAs, and quiz fields."
msgstr "A form-tag is a short code enclosed in square brackets used in a form content. A form-tag generally represents an input field, and its components can be separated into four parts: type, name, options, and values. Contact Form 7 supports several types of form-tags including text fields, number fields, date fields, checkboxes, radio buttons, menus, file-uploading fields, CAPTCHAs, and quiz fields."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:81
msgid "<strong>Additional Settings</strong> provides a place where you can customize the behavior of this contact form by adding code snippets."
msgstr "<strong>Additional Settings</strong> provides a place where you can customise the behaviour of this contact form by adding code snippets."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:80
msgid "In <strong>Messages</strong>, you can edit various types of messages used for this contact form. These messages are relatively short messages, like a validation error message you see when you leave a required field blank."
msgstr "In <strong>Messages</strong>, you can edit various types of messages used for this contact form. These messages are relatively short messages, like a validation error message you see when you leave a required field blank."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:79
msgid "<strong>Mail (2)</strong> is an additional mail template that works similar to Mail. Mail (2) is different in that it is sent only when Mail has been sent successfully."
msgstr "<strong>Mail (2)</strong> is an additional mail template that works similarly to Mail. Mail (2) is different in that it is sent only when Mail has been sent successfully."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:78
msgid "<strong>Mail</strong> manages a mail template (headers and message body) that this contact form will send when users submit it. You can use Contact Form 7&#8217;s mail-tags here."
msgstr "<strong>Mail</strong> manages a mail template (headers and message body) that this contact form will send when users submit it. You can use Contact Form 7&#8217;s mail-tags here."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:77
msgid "<strong>Form</strong> is a content of HTML form. You can use arbitrary HTML, which is allowed inside a form element. You can also use Contact Form 7&#8217;s form-tags here."
msgstr "<strong>Form</strong> is a content of an HTML form. You can use arbitrary HTML, which is allowed inside a form element. You can also use Contact Form 7&#8217;s form-tags here."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:76
msgid "<strong>Title</strong> is the title of a contact form. This title is only used for labeling a contact form, and can be edited."
msgstr "<strong>Title</strong> is the title of a contact form. This title is only used for labelling a contact form, and can be edited."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:75
msgid "On this screen, you can edit a contact form. A contact form is comprised of the following components:"
msgstr "On this screen, you can edit a contact form. A contact form is comprised of the following components:"

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:73
msgid "<strong>Duplicate</strong> - Clones that contact form. A cloned contact form inherits all content from the original, but has a different ID."
msgstr "<strong>Duplicate</strong> - Clones that contact form. A cloned contact form inherits all content from the original, but has a different ID."

#: admin/includes/help-tabs.php:72
msgid "<strong>Edit</strong> - Navigates to the editing screen for that contact form. You can also reach that screen by clicking on the contact form title."
msgstr "<strong>Edit</strong> - Navigates to the editing screen for that contact form. You can also reach that screen by clicking on the contact form title."

